A||||11||deceler8||More Computer Help Needed...||||1||
Z||000000||deceler8||09-01-2000||09:19 AM||||I just picked up a cheap laptop and need some help. The previous owner deleted all his files as well as his Web browser and Internet access program.<P>This computer doesn't have a CD drive on it and I don't think anyone puts MS Internet Explorer or Netscape on 3.5's anymore, so how do I get these programs on the computer ?<P>Is it possible to copy them from my desktop PC to this laptop, and if so, how ?<P>Both computers have Windows 95 on them.<P>Any help is greatly appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||whamel||09-01-2000||09:37 AM||||You didn't mention anything about a network card in the laptop, so I'll assume you don't have a home network.  (If you do, you can do an 'install later' download of IE on your home machine, share the directory and install it that way.)<BR>The easiest way to get a web browser on the machine is to dial into the internet, go to a dos prompt, run FTP, open ftp.netscape.com (I think this still works), set your properties to BIN, change into the directory where netscape puts their binaries, and download it.  It'll take forever if you're using a modem, but it will work.  I can break the process down in e-mail for you if you want.<BR>I can also give you some other ideas if this doesn't work out for you.  I have to do this kind of stuff all the time.  (Hey!  something I really know something about! &lt;grin&gt; )<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||09-01-2000||09:53 AM||||You can also do a search on the internet for a program called "lap link" it will enable you to talk to another computer via the printer ports. The program will fit on one floppy so you can put it on the laptop. <BR>If you have a hard time finding it let me know. I have a shareware version at work and can Email it to you. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||whamel||09-01-2000||10:35 AM||||Laplink's a good idea too!  Either way would solve your problem.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||peterh||09-01-2000||10:46 AM||||What about buying an external cd rom, I think they can attach tru the parallel port. Try computer shows or mail order for cheap stuff.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||09-01-2000||11:20 AM||||Man, I forgot about Laplink...<P>What can I say but...You guys are good !||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-01-2000||12:59 PM||||Parralel port CD players work but they can be a pain. Performance of these is not that great so don't plan on playing games from CD but they will at least load files for you.<P>If you have the PCMCIA/PCCARD slots working then you would be better with the more expencive CD players that plug into there. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||09-01-2000||03:14 PM||||Don't you need a special cable for LapLink? You can by a special USB-cable that comes with a program called "Smart-Link". That works pretty good too.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||09-01-2000||03:30 PM||||Cliff is right- you need a "parallel port data transer cable"- most vendors sell them because win95+ has a way of linking up with it, but I have never got it to work. So, I just use the old DOS version of LapLink.<P>------------------<BR>The slower they think you are, the more suprised they will be when you smoke them.||||reg||1
Z||000009||deceler8||09-02-2000||10:09 AM||||Well, I ended up downloading a shareware program called Fast PC Linker III...worked like a charm.<P>With this program I was able to copy programs from my desktop CDROM right to my laptop. I did need to buy a cable, but it was about $8<P>Thanks to everyone for the fast replies.<P>And thanks Ogre...your piece on power decklid installation was right on the money. Put the option on my car in 20 minutes using your instructions. Wish everything on this car was that easy.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||09-02-2000||02:22 PM||||You're welcome. I wish they were all that easy too. The only other one that's close is fixing the temperature gauge wire. I did that one durring a lunch break. Including eating.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||09-02-2000||10:34 PM||||Laplink.. now there's a blast from the past!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
